30:04.620 --> 30:07.760
but structurally they play entirely different roles.

30:07.880 --> 30:09.240
They belong to dual spaces.

30:09.660 --> 30:15.360
If V is your space of vectors, the dual space V star is the space of all linear functionals,

30:15.920 --> 30:19.240
max that take a vector as an input and output a single scalar number.

30:19.240 --> 30:23.000
So a vector is an arrow, indicating a direction and magnitude of flow.

30:23.380 --> 30:26.460
A co-vector is the functional environment that the vector pierces through.

